    "Totterdown is typically more expensive than Knowle. Its small Victorian terraced houses sit on some of the steepest streets in the country, but Temple Meads is a walk of around fifteen minutes and the city centre is close. It has a strong community and arts scene, but very few shops, bars or restaurants.",
    "Knowle offers larger houses, many with gardens, and a more suburban atmosphere, with parks such as Redcatch Park and Perrett's Park. The Wells Road provides frequent buses and everyday shopping, but traffic and air quality along it are a concern. Knowle West, to the south-west, has significant deprivation. Knowle's streets also sit higher and further from the river, so its hills are longer if not quite as steep as Totterdown's, and walking into town is a much bigger commitment.",
